**TRACK: House of the Rising Sun**
key: Am | tempo: 120 | swing: 0% | subdivision: 8th

[intro]
Chords: Am | C | D | F | Am | E | Am | E
Melody: (arpeggiated, 8th notes) A2-C3-E3-A3 | C3-E3-G3-C4 | D3-F#3-A3-D4 | F2-A2-C3-F3 | A2-C3-E3-A3 | E2-G#3-B3-E4 | A2-C3-E3-A3 | E2-G#3-B3-E4
@player: guitar (fingerpicked, arpeggios), bass (root notes on 1 & 3), no drums

[verse1]
Chords: Am | C | D | F | Am | E | Am | E
Melody: (vocal line, quarter+8th) A3 A3 B3 C4 | C4 C4 D4 E4 | D4 D4 F#4 A4 | F4 F4 E4 D4 | C4 C4 B3 A3 | B3 B3 G#3 E3 | A3 A3 B3 C4 | B3 G#3 E3 (hold)
Lyrics:
There is a house in New Orleans
They call the Rising Sun
And it's been the ruin of many a poor boy
And God, I know I'm one
@player: guitar (same arpeggio pattern), bass (root notes), vocals (lead, folk ballad tone)

[verse2]
Chords: Am | C | D | F | Am | E | Am | E
Melody: (same as verse1, slight variation) A3 A3 B3 C4 | C4 C4 D4 E4 | D4 D4 F#4 A4 | F4 F4 E4 D4 | C4 C4 B3 A3 | B3 B3 G#3 E3 | A3 A3 B3 C4 | B3 G#3 E3 (hold)
Lyrics:
My mother was a tailor
She sewed my new blue jeans
My father was a gamblin' man
Down in New Orleans
@player: guitar (same), bass (same), vocals (same)

[chorus]
Chords: F | E | Am | C | D | F | Am | E
Melody: (higher, more sustained) F4 F4 E4 D4 | E4 E4 D4 C4 | C4 B3 A3 B3 | C4 C4 D4 E4 | D4 D4 F#4 A4 | F4 F4 E4 D4 | C4 B3 A3 B3 | B3 G#3 E3 (hold)
Lyrics:
Oh, mother, tell your children
Not to do what I have done
Spend your lives in sin and misery
In the House of the Rising Sun
@player: guitar (adds light strum on downbeats), bass (walking lines), vocals (chorus, slightly louder)

[outro]
Chords: Am | C | D | F | Am | E | Am (hold)
Melody: (instrumental, repeat intro arpeggio, final Am chord sustained)
@player: guitar (arpeggios fade out), bass (root notes, final low A), no vocals
